		(uuid "5333cd5f-276f-4751-a27b-28f86f764542")
	)
	(text "why? you can change this\nin the lab as per performance.\nalso, according to voltage\ndivision, this is a good\nstarting point"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 123.952 82.55 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.508 0.508)
			)
		)
		(uuid "61e749db-8330-47d7-8f54-ab775bc9f6ed")
	)
	(text "why 5k1?\nbecause we're already\nusing 5k1 for USB CCx\npins, and this is to\nmake a better BOM."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 151.384 83.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.508 0.508)
			)
		)
		(uuid "67b19f62-b9b7-4fb0-a459-86349e695f6e")
	)
	(text "For any connector or exposed interface\nyou typically should add ESD protection\nto make sure when you're messing around\nwith the board you don't accidentally\nfry your devices.\nHowever, phil says that from his experience\nthese ST mcus are pretty resilient, so\nit's fine for *test boards* to skip them, however\nhe doesn't recommend this for connectors\non commercial boards"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 178.816 122.174 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
		)
		(uuid "9d9e9069-c25c-47b8-b9c8-a8e942cc41ff")
	)
